      "cve": "CVE-2026-126347",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-126347"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "Tornado is a Python web framework and asynchronous networking library. In versions through 6.6.0, applications using   tornado.web.RedirectHandler   with URL templates that allow attacker-controlled substitutions to influence the destination can be vulnerable to an open redirect using three or more leading slashes. Differences between Python's URL parsing and browser URL interpretation allow a crafted destination to redirect a user to an attacker-controlled host. The remediation for CVE-2026-116578 in version 6.6.0 did not fully address this case. This issue is fixed in version 6.6.1.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
